  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Controlled-evaluation prerequisites</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>One bounded AI-assisted workflow</li>
      <li>Representative outbound request and provider response</li>
      <li>Intended enterprise action and correlation requirements</li>
      <li>Request and result ALLOW/DENY cases</li>
      <li>Evidence, reconstruction, replay, report, and export requirements</li>
      <li>Deployment assumptions and identity-provider context</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Customer-specific architecture-fit memos and sample mappings are
      controlled-access outputs of a Controlled Evaluation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>What reviewers can assess</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>How Request Admission Authorization returns ALLOW or DENY</li>
      <li>
        How Result-to-Action Authorization applies to a declared intended action
      </li>
      <li>How Active Verified Releases govern evaluation</li>
      <li>What related Verifiable Decision Records contain</li>
      <li>That Verify is read-only and cannot grant runtime authority</li>
      <li>That AI-assisted insights are non-authoritative</li>
      <li>Where customer and BeaconGuard responsibilities divide</li>
      <li>What remains out of scope for BeaconGuard</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="page-actions">
